  "chapters": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "html": "\n    \n    <p><em>It was right before your eyes: a vessel, shimmering in the dark. It was forming, shifting, a voice booming all around you. </em></p><p><em>You said it was beautiful. It was kind. It liked sour things. </em></p><p><em>Its appearance shifted, from grey to green to blue and pink. One moment, it was long and tall, then short and squat, and it kept changing, its limbs reshaping, its clothing growing and shrinking, its hair dancing around in the void. It was your creation. You were so proud. </em></p><p><em>Your eyes were drawn to the SOUL at its center. It was glowing, a beautiful, aching red. You watched in wonder as the SOUL then began to change colour, shifting to cyan, to orange, to green, continuing the rainbow. Its light was spread all around. Just by staring at it, you could feel its power. It was the Angel. </em><b><em>You </em></b><em>were the Angel, your power shifting and changing.</em></p><p><em>Then your vessel was discarded. </em></p><p><em>You could not choose your fate. You couldn't feel your hand. </em></p><p><em>Everything went black.</em></p><p>...</p><p>...</p><hr><p>I felt a tugging at my chest.</p><p>I couldn't see a thing. Cold, thick darkness surrounded me. I took a deep breath.</p><p>I clenched my hands over my heart; a cyan SOUL emerged. It glowed in front of me, radiating with power. I was entranced; the soft shimmer surrounded me, almost like a hug. It was warm and patient, unexpectedly calming. I was comfortable. I wanted to stay like that, forever.</p><p>\"<b>YOUR TIME IS RUNNING OUT, FAYE RIBSON.</b>\"</p><p>I peered into the darkness. I couldn't see the source of the voice, but I could <em>feel</em> It. I could feel It down to my core, to my very heart. It was watching me. Holding me.</p><p>\"<b>USE THE POWER YOU HAVE BEEN GIVEN</b>,\" HE told me. \"<b>PLAY YOUR ROLE. PROTECT THEM, AND GIVE YOUR SOUL TO THE CAUSE.</b>\"</p><p>I nodded. The darkness kept growing. So, so dark. Darker, yet darker. My eyes burned. The warmth vanished, replaced by the icy cold of reality.</p><p>I tried to breathe, but my lungs were deflating, like there was a hole inside them. My skin was freezing, like ice was growing over it. It was so cold. I was so tired. I didn't want to wake up.</p><p>My eyes finally opened, greeting the pale timber of the ceiling. I could hear my phone buzzing on my desk. I sat up, slowly, painfully, reaching for it. My joints creaked, making my eyes water.</p><p>I hoped my boyfriend, Brayden, was ringing. He often messaged me in the morning, sending a selfie from his cross-country club, or whatever else he was up to. Sometimes Noelle and Jockington would be in the picture, too. Noelle was usually a bit shy, but she always seemed to enjoy herself at the club. It was nice to see her happy, after all she'd been through. Brayden was just like that, uplifting others with his presence alone. His smile was enough to make me feel hope, to make me feel like I <em>mattered</em>. (Which was why I couldn't tell him the truth...)</p><p>Sadly, he was out of town for the day, going to his sister's wedding. I was on my own.</p><p>My face fell when I saw the actual caller ID. I didn't want to pick up the phone. I didn't want to talk about <em>that</em>.</p><p>I knew I couldn't avoid it forever, though. At some point, I'd have to answer the phone.</p><p>But for the moment... if I could wait, so could she. I slowly dragged myself out of bed. It was getting harder to move each day, both physically and emotionally. Before long, I wouldn't be able to move much longer. At least I actually got to sleep at home for the night... but I knew I'd have to go back to the hospital before long.</p><p>I reached out, grabbing my medication off my bedside desk. I counted out the small, white tablets, grabbing the glass of water beside them. I swallowed, before sitting back on my bed, closing my eyes once again. I was glad my mattress was so soft. I could sit there all day.</p><p>I gazed over at the other side of the room. My sibling, Kris, was still asleep. Despite my sluggish body, they somehow still managed to out-sleep me. Our brother, Asriel, wasn't here to drag them out of bed, and even if I tried, they wouldn't listen to me.</p><p>I heard a knock on our door. Mom invited herself in, opening the curtains.</p><p>\"Kris, Faye, time to wake up,\" she chorused, \"or you will be late for school!\"</p><p>She turned to Kris, who walked out of bed. Immediately, I knew it wasn't them. Their walk was strangely stiff, their arms glued to their sides. Their footsteps were too noisy. They wouldn't even be able to try to sneak up on me. They were already wearing their clothes, as they didn't want to get ch\n<div class=\"chapter preface group\">\n      <div class=\"end notes module\" id=\"chapter_1_endnotes\">\n        <h3 class=\"heading\">Notes:</h3>\n        <blockquote class=\"userstuff\">\n          <p>A/N: The SOUL: I always come back....</p>\n<p>So... Kris and Faye are siblings now. I went back and forth on who I wanted Faye to live with, but I went with them being Kris' sibling as I thought it'd be the most interesting. :) Toriel would def take in another orphan haha. Also they're not twins, despite what Susie says. They'd be around the same age tho.</p>\n<p>I feel like I neglected Kris (and Faye) a lot in the original Deltagroup so they're gonna get a lot more focus here lol. Also sorry to that one person who wanted Chara to appear but they're probably not gonna show up. I love Chara and all but Kris deserves to shine on their own. And also there are wayyy too many characters already lord help me 😭😭😭 Idk unless Toby throws Chara in as the chapter 7 secret boss dhhxjwjsujd. A bit late but Happy 10 years of Undertale! The stream was awesome, I loved the lore Gerson shared... very interesting. 👀</p>\n        </blockquote>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n",
