      "number": 2,
      "html": "\n    \n    <p><em>The floor was cold. You opened your eyes. </em></p><p><em>You were controlling Kris. You tried to switch to your other vessel, but narration stated there was 'only darkness'. </em></p><p><em>You saw Melody beside you, and a shining star ahead. A shining star, that reminded you of a world you'd been before...</em></p><p><em>You reached out, and you SAVED.</em></p><hr><p>I woke up in a bed. Good news, it wasn't a hospital bed. Bad news, it was somewhere I'd never been before.</p><p>The walls were black stone, lit up by beautiful, flaming blue torches. My bed was incredibly soft; easily the comfiest bed I'd ever slept on. I could've kept sleeping.</p><p>I heard soft footsteps; a hooded, cloaked figure was approaching. I couldn't see their face. They gasped when they noticed I was awake.</p><p>\"Oh, you're up!\" they said, rushing to my side. \"How are you feeling?\"</p><p>\"No worse than usual...\" I admitted.</p><p>\"Is there, um, anything you need?\" they asked. \"Would you like some water? Or something to eat? I just baked a cake!\"</p><p>\"Cake sounds nice,\" I replied.</p><p>The figure hurried out of the room, returning a few moments later with a tray, which held a slice of strawberry sponge cake and a pot of green tea.</p><p>They helped by pouring the tea into a mug, then offering it to me.</p><p>\"Thank you,\" I said, sipping the tea. It was hot enough to be comforting, but not burning.</p><p>\"Of course!\" the figure said, dipping their head. \"I'm... I'm just so glad you're here. It's ever so wonderful to meet you, Faye.\"</p><p>\"Who are you?\" I asked.</p><p>The figure slowly removed their hood, revealing a pitch-black monster-like Darkner, with fluffy ears and glasses. He was wearing a green, witch-like hat, as well as a green robe and a pink scarf.</p><p>\"Welcome,\" he said. \"I am the Prince of this Kingdom... the KINGDOM of DARKNESS.\"</p><p>\"Oh,\" I breathed.</p><p>\"My name is Ralsei,\" he told me. \"I hope we can be good friends!\"</p><p>I offered my free hand for him to shake; his grip was soft and warm, like a teddy bear's. It reminded me of my family.</p><p>\"What is this place?\" I asked him. \"This... 'Kingdom of Darkness'?\"</p><p>\"Well...\" Ralsei dipped his head. \"This is the Dark World, inside the closet. The darkness... created by the hopes and dreams of Lightners.\"</p><p>\"I see,\" I said. \"Where is everyone else?\"</p><p>\"I'm not sure,\" Ralsei admitted. \"I'm sure they're on their way, though. I can sense them from the west.\"</p><p>\"How did I end up here?\" I asked.</p><p>\"I found you, in the center of town,\" he said. \"You were unconscious, so I brought you inside.\"</p><p>\"Oh... \" I replied. \"Thank you.\"</p><p>\"Of course,\" he smiled, showing fangs. \"Anything you need, I'm here to help.\"</p><p>I stared at my hands. My skin was stark white - somehow even more pale than it usually was. I felt my cheek; a bandaid was covering the scar on my cheek. The hair on my shoulder was a dark cyan, almost glimmering in the pale light.</p><p>\"There is a legend in this land,\" Ralsei told me. \"The legend of DELTARUNE. It tells of... um, well, maybe we should wait until the others get here. Unless you want to hear it now? It's up to you.\"</p><p>\"I'm okay with waiting,\" I said, softly.</p><p>Ralsei nodded. \"Okay!\" He sat on the chair beside my bed. \"Um... how's the cake?\"</p><p>I took a slice of it. It was delicious; creamy and sweet, with the juiciness of the strawberries an added bonus. And yet, it didn't feel very... filling. It was almost like eating cotton-candy; the food simply disappeared as soon as you swallowed.</p><p>\"It's yummy,\" I said.</p><p>\"I'm glad to hear it,\" Ralsei told me. \"Is there anything you'd like? Some more tea?\"</p><p>\"I...\" My voice trailed off.</p><p>\"Oh, am I being too much?\" Ralsei stood up. \"Sorry. I... I'm a prince, but I don't have any subjects. I... I've just been waiting so long for you and your friends to arrive.\"</p><p>\"It's alright,\" I assured him. \"I'm just... I want to enjoy the time I have. That's all.\" I looked at him. \"Us arriving is part of the prophecy, right?\"</p><p>\"Right,\" Ralsei replied. \"Everything \n</body></html>",
